Z||000002||william_thorniii||02-25-2000||11:15 AM||||Super X:<P>email: superX@supernet.com<BR>webpage: <A HREF="http://users.supernet.com" TARGET=_blank>http://users.supernet.com</A> <P>Super X doesn't usually sell cars, but unless I am mistaken presently is selling his own 88 GT with T-Tops.<P>Fiero Dave:<P>e-mail: fierodave@webtv.net <BR>webpage: <A HREF="http://fierodave.dreamwater.com" TARGET=_blank>http://fierodave.dreamwater.com</A>  <P>Dave is great at finding good Fieros at great prices.  <P>Ed Parks:<P>e-mail: fierofactory@juno.com<BR>He is out of town on Fiero deliveries this week though.. so don't expect his usual lightening quick response.  Ed is the "Father of the Modern Day Fiero" in my opinion.  He is a mechanic by trade and can do just about ANYTHING that you want.  <P>Paul Vargyas:<P>e-mail: paulv@xnet.com<BR>webpage: <A HREF="http://www.xnet.com/~paulv/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xnet.com/~paulv/</A>  <P>Paul is a member of NIFE and seems to find some good cars now and again.  He doesn't buy/sell nearly as many as Fiero Dave or Ed though.  <P>Hope this helps,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000003||V6pack||02-25-2000||01:34 PM||||MooCow, I know you are in another neck of the woods(I'm in Ca.)but I have an '87GT T-top auto you can see on Fierodave's site. It is in "fair/good" condition and would sure go cheaper than $5K. <P>I have used the same no middleman shipper for 3 cross country car hauls and he is reliable & reasonable.<BR>My $.02 Good Luck<BR>v6pack||||reg||12
